  "final_response": "I did it. Here's what happened in this turn:\n\n**The skepticism:** The Clarity Library was clinically sound but emotionally barren — six essays, guides, checklists, and one play, all about efficiency without ever demonstrating why anyone should *care*. A folklorist knows that people don't remember frameworks. They remember stories.\n\n**The contribution (Issue 06):** I wrote \"The Keeper of Names\" — a folk tale about a village where everyone forgot everything, and a girl who helped them by pruning their lists down to the single sentences that would make them weep years later. The story itself practices radical clarity: every detail exists only to earn its final line (*She called you Mama before she knew what a mother was*).\n\n**The structural changes:**\n- **issue_06.md** — new file, the folk tale\n- **reading_path.md** — inserted Issue 06 at Stage 4, proving clarity's emotional arc\n- **index.md** — added Issue 06 to both Essays and Dramatic Works sections\n\nThe library now demonstrates clarity in three modes: technical (Issue 05), narrative (Issue 06), and dramatic (A Study in Signal). The arc is complete.",
